runtime.py
context.py
orchestrator.py
lifecycle.py

exceptions.py
types.py

execution/
tools/
events/
guardrails/
```

---

# Module Overview

## agent.py

Main autonomous agent implementation.

Responsibilities

- start agent
- stop agent
- execute requests
- manage sessions
- communicate with orchestrator

---

## runtime.py

Controls runtime initialization.

Responsibilities

- startup
- shutdown
- dependency initialization
- resource management

---

## lifecycle.py

Controls state transitions.

Example

```
Created

↓

Initialized

↓

Running

↓

Paused

↓

Stopped

↓

Shutdown
```

---

## context.py

Shared execution context.

Contains

- configuration
- memory handles
- blockchain clients
- RPC manager
- logger
- session state
- execution metadata

---

## orchestrator.py

Central coordinator.

Responsibilities

- receive tasks
- select tools
- invoke execution pipeline
- collect results
- publish events

---

## execution/

Responsible for task execution.

Contains

- executor
- scheduler
- retry engine
- task queue

---

## tools/

Responsible for tool management.

Contains

- registry
- router
- loader
- validator

---

## guardrails/

Provides runtime protection.

Includes

- permission checks
- policy engine
- sandbox
- risk engine

---

## events/

Implements event-driven architecture.

Contains

- event bus
- dispatcher
- event types

---

# Execution Flow

```
Incoming Request
        │
        ▼
Agent
        │
        ▼
Orchestrator
        │
        ▼
Guardrails
        │
        ▼
Tool Router
        │
        ▼
Execution Engine
        │
        ▼
Blockchain/API/Memory
        │
        ▼
Result
        │
        ▼
Event Bus
        │
        ▼
Response
```

---

# Design Principles

The Core package follows these principles:

- Modular
- Async-first
- Event-driven
- Strong typing
- Dependency injection
- Low coupling
- High cohesion
- Fault tolerant
- Observable
- Security-first

---

# Security Responsibilities

The Core module never:

- stores private keys
- signs transactions directly
- bypasses guardrails
- exposes secrets
- executes unvalidated tools

All sensitive operations must pass through:

- Security Layer
- Validation Layer
- Guardrails
- Audit Logging

---

# Error Handling

Every execution path supports

- retries
- timeout handling
- cancellation
- graceful shutdown
- structured exceptions
- audit logging

---

